  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Justice obligated $337M in FY2027 to date, across 3,061 awards with an average award size of $110K. Obligations fell 96.7% year over year. Historical annual obligations show a much larger baseline: FY22 was $9B, FY23 was $10B, FY24 was $9.3B, FY25 was $8.5B, and FY26 was $10.3B. The FY2027 to date total is concentrated in a handful of categories and vendors, with Security Guards and Patrol Services accounting for $119M of obligations and METROPOLITAN SECURITY SERVICES, INC. receiving $102M. Other notable categories include General Medical and Surgical Hospitals at $39.5M and All Other Legal Services at $18.2M. Other vendors with meaningful FY2027 to date obligations include NAPHCARE LLC at $22M and FORFEITURE SUPPORT ASSOCIATES LLC at $16.3M. This year to date data is a partial view; FY2027 totals are fiscal year to date and may change as the year progresses.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Why are FY2027 to date obligations much lower than prior years?",
        "body": "The Department of Justice obligated $337M in FY2027 to date, compared with single-year totals of $9B, $10B, $9.3B, $8.5B, and $10.3B in FY22 through FY26. Obligations fell 96.7% year over year. The FY2027 figure is a fiscal year to date total, not a full fiscal year tally. The award count for FY2027 to date is 3,061 with an average award size of $110K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which vendors and NAICS categories dominate FY2027 to date obligations?",
        "body": "Security Guards and Patrol Services is the largest category at $119M, followed by General Medical and Surgical Hospitals at $39.5M and All Other Legal Services at $18.2M. METROPOLITAN SECURITY SERVICES, INC. is the top vendor at $102M, followed by NAPHCARE LLC at $22M and FORFEITURE SUPPORT ASSOCIATES LLC at $16.3M. Several other vendors and categories contribute smaller amounts, including MCKESSON CORPORATION at $14.5M and Software Publishers at $10.5M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of Justice spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Justice obligated $337M on contracts in FY2027 to date. The Department of Justice recorded 3,061 awards in FY2027 to date with an average award size of $110K, and obligations fell 96.7% year over year. Historical annual obligations were $9B in FY22, $10B in FY23, $9.3B in FY24, $8.5B in FY25, and $10.3B in FY26."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Justice buy?",
      "a": "Justice buys security, medical, legal, food, pharmaceutical, care, aviation support, and software services; the top category is Security Guards and Patrol Services at $119M. Other top categories are General Medical and Surgical Hospitals at $39.5M, All Other Legal Services at $18.2M, All Other Miscellaneous Food Manufacturing at $16.5M, and Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing at $14.6M."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are Justice's largest contractors?",
      "a": "METROPOLITAN SECURITY SERVICES, INC. is Justice's largest contractor at $102M. Other top contractors are NAPHCARE LLC at $22M, FORFEITURE SUPPORT ASSOCIATES LLC at $16.3M, MCKESSON CORPORATION at $14.5M, and AAR AIRCRAFT SERVICES, INC. at $12.4M."
